lessons.body:
Cache Optimism: onMutate, Snapshot
and Rollback
Phase 25 - Optimistic Updates

Volume 07 - Advanced Application Architecture

When cache optimism is justified
If multiple components observe the same Task detail cache, changing only the initiating button is
insufficient. Then TaskFlow may optimistically patch the shared detail cache.

The four-step pattern
onMutate: async (status, context) => {
const key = taskKeys.detail(taskId)

await context.client.cancelQueries({
queryKey: key,
})

const previous =
context.client.getQueryData<Task>(key)

context.client.setQueryData<Task>(
key,
old => old ? { ...old, status } : old,
)

return { previous }
}

Rollback
onError: (_error, _status, rollback, context) => {
if (rollback?.previous) {
context.client.setQueryData(
taskKeys.detail(taskId),
rollback.previous,
)
}
}

What the snapshot means
The snapshot is not a second permanent source of truth. It is temporary rollback material
associated with that mutation attempt.

