lessons.body:
Server Reconciliation: onSuccess,
onSettled and Invalidation
Phase 25 - Optimistic Updates

Volume 07 - Advanced Application Architecture

Optimism ends when the server responds
The local prediction must eventually be replaced or confirmed by server truth. TaskFlow uses the
returned Task when useful, then invalidates affected lists so authorization, filtering, derived state,
timestamps, and business rules are re-evaluated by the backend.

Reconcile detail immediately
onSuccess: (serverTask, _status, _rollback, context) => {
context.client.setQueryData(
taskKeys.detail(taskId),
serverTask,
)
}

Then invalidate authoritative collections
onSettled: async (_data, _error, _status, _rollback, context) => {
await Promise.all([
context.client.invalidateQueries({
queryKey: taskKeys.detail(taskId),
}),
context.client.invalidateQueries({
queryKey: taskKeys.lists(),
}),
])
}

Awaiting invalidation
TanStack Query keeps the mutation pending while an awaited callback Promise is unresolved. That
can be useful when the UI should not announce “saved” until reconciliation has started/completed
according to your policy.

